#### preserves a hyphenated word in a full-line comment verbatim

- Verify: preserves a hyphenated word in a full-line comment verbatim


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 8 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: preserves a hyphenated word in a full-line comment verbatim")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
"""Regression: add_expression_spacing used to run on comment lines
too, rewriting `pure-Simple` to `pure - Simple` and tripping the
formatter's own lexical-equivalence guard (fixed 2026-07-17; see
doc/08_tracking/bug/host_toolchain_seed_pinned_lint_fmt_doccov_unrunnable_2026-07-17.md)."""
val out = formatted_or_fail("# a pure-Simple comment\nfn add(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64:\n    a + b\n")
assert_contains(out, "# a pure-Simple comment")
```

</details>

#### is idempotent: formatting already-formatted source changes nothing

- Verify: is idempotent: formatting already-formatted source changes nothing


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: is idempotent: formatting already-formatted source changes nothing")
val once = formatted_or_fail("fn add(a:i64,b:i64)->i64:\n    a+b\n")
val twice = formatted_or_fail(once)
assert_equal(once, twice)
```

</details>

